md += ['## Architecture tradeoffs','','C launches one FFmpeg validator per input plus the final render (N+1 child launches). C++, Go and Rust attach one-frame decoded validation outputs to one FFmpeg render. All four publish by exclusive hard link or atomic overwrite rename, avoid a second output copy, and pin input descriptors. Zig fresh publication copies a completed temporary into an exclusively created final destination. Node sequentially launches ffprobe and FFmpeg for each input (2N audio-tool child launches), then retains whole decoded/rendered tracks and encoded bytes in memory; it fsyncs before publication. These are orchestration, validation, buffering and durability differences, not a language-only DSP benchmark.','', 'Rust uses a 50 ms fallback poll timeout; observed bimodal short-launch latency is consistent with that process-wait path. This is a source-informed interpretation, not an isolated causal experiment. The fixed candidate source was not tuned after results.','', 'CLI syntax checks for Node exercise the canonical adapter. The baseline receives translated linked speed arguments in the same Node process; no audio transforms or encoders were inserted by the adapter.','']
